<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vaballathus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 267–272</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vaballathus was the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odaenathus">Odaenathus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zenobia">Zenobia</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palmyra">Palmyra</a>, in whose name his mother ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palmyrene-empire">Palmyrene Empire</a> after his father's murder in 267. Under Zenobia's regency Palmyra took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a>, and in 272 Vaballathus was proclaimed Augustus. The emperor Aurelian defeated the Palmyrenes that year and captured Zenobia; the fate of Vaballathus is unknown.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vaballathus.jpg" alt="Vaballathus" width="320" height="309" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aurelian-with-vabalathus_(reverse).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
